## Goal
Visualize the principal component structure of the six RNA-seq samples, colored by treatment condition (untreated vs. treated). PCA will reveal sample relationships and whether the first two principal components separate the experimental groups.

## Inputs
Artifact types resolve through each sub-stage's OUTPUTS.tsv at execution time; the paths
below are what they resolve to today.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| counts_gene | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |
| design | 01_prepare_samplesheets | 01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv |

## Method
1. Load gene count matrix from `counts_gene` and sample design from design CSV using Python (scikit-learn, pandas, seaborn, matplotlib). Environment: gars-bio.
2. Filter genes retaining those with ≥5 counts in ≥3 samples.
3. Log2-transform count data after adding pseudocount of 1 (log2(counts + 1)).
4. Apply PCA with scikit-learn's PCA (n_components=2) to the transposed matrix (samples as rows, genes as columns).
5. Generate scatter plot of PC1 vs PC2, coloring points by condition from design; mark replicate numbers as labels; include explained variance on axes.
6. Export PC scores (sample coordinates on PC1/PC2) as a CSV table.
7. Script location: scripts/pca_analysis.py

